"""The lever registry: every lever the modes (modes.py) name, described from the kit files that implement it (file:line under boltz2/opt/).

A lever is one runtime optimization with its own switch, applied by the kit's own code inside the worker process. This registry describes;
it never applies. ``switch`` is the environment name the kit reads, ``value`` the setting the mode rows use, ``kit_gate`` the kit's own
run-time fallback (what makes the lever inert on a box — reported as ``levers_fallback`` from the worker log).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

from typing import Dict

